  "id": 203986044946940,
  "uuid": "a04bfcae-8dc8-43bb-a4a4-52376b72989e",
  "is_folder": false,
  "content": {
    "_uid": "75f4260c-5ce4-60a2-b9f1-c3cf5233c032",
    "body": [
      {
        "_uid": "425383b9-0cb6-9234-1c1e-e1a351f2d958",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Dr Akram, who holds a PhD in Statistics from Monash University with a focus on time-series analysis and forecasting, brought a wealth of expertise to the seminar. He commenced the session by illuminating the essential nature of secondary data, emphasizing its role as a valuable complement to primary data in the research landscape. Drawing on his experience, Dr Akram discussed the biases and limitations inherent in working with secondary data, shedding light on key considerations for researchers navigating this terrain.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "One of the session's highlights was Dr. Akram's insightful exploration of the challenges faced by students and young researchers as they embark on their research journeys. Attendees were provided with valuable guidance on overcoming these challenges, ensuring a more robust and nuanced approach to utilizing secondary data for research purposes. Dr. Akram's emphasis on mitigating potential pitfalls in the research process resonated with the diverse audience, comprised of faculty, students, and enthusiastic alumni from AKU-IED.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Beyond simply identifying challenges, Dr Akram actively engaged with educators, sharing practical insights on how to conduct effective secondary analysis. He delved into the tools and methodologies that can enhance the validity and reliability of research outcomes. The session proved to be a valuable resource for educators seeking to integrate secondary data analysis into their research methodologies, offering a roadmap to navigate complexities and extract meaningful insights.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The Kazim Bachhus Research Seminar series continues to be a beacon of intellectual exploration, offering a platform for thought leaders to share their insights and experiences. The latest session, exploring the nuanced world of secondary data analysis, not only enriched the academic community at AKU-IED but also resonated with a wider audience, fostering a collaborative spirit in the pursuit of knowledge and research excellence.",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
