    "show_share": true,
    "description": "In a stimulating session of the Kazim Bacchus Research Seminar series hosted by AKU-IED, attendees delved into the intricacies of analyzing secondary data, discovering both the opportunities and challenges inherent in this research approach. The event, which took place on Wednesday, January 24, 2024, featured Dr Muhammad Akram, a distinguished research fellow and bio-statistician from the Merry Mackillop Institute of Health Research (MMIHR) at the Australian Catholic University, Melbourne.",
